# RTL Implementation Plan

## Coding rules
- Synthesizable Verilog-2001 unless the supplied flow requires otherwise.
- One clock domain, active-high synchronous reset.
- No generated clocks, simulation delays, or testbench constructs in RTL.
- Avoid inferred latches.
- Do not write RTL until P1 decisions are resolved.

## Proposed tree
```text
rtl/
  pump_protection_controller.v
tb/
  pump_protection_controller_tb.v
simulation/
reports/
constraints/
```
Start with one RTL module unless splitting it provides a clear benefit.

## Checkpoints
- P0: proposal and scope; proposal submitted (user-reported).
- P1: freeze interface, FSM, timer semantics, fault-clear policy, reset and corner cases.
- P2: implement RTL from frozen architecture.
- P3: compile/lint; review all warnings.
- P4: self-checking simulation passes.
- P5: safety/corner-case regression passes.
- P6: synthesis baseline and area statistics.
- P7: identify actual platform/PDK and constraints.
- P8: floorplan and power planning.
- P9: placement.
- P10: CTS if required.
- P11: STA and critical-path review.
- P12: routing.
- P13: DRC/LVS checks supported by the flow.
- P14: verify generated GDS and record exact path/results.
- P15: final report and demonstration.

## Gate rule
Do not advance merely because a command ran. Require the checkpoint's evidence and acceptance criteria. A failure returns the project to the relevant fix-and-retest step.

## P1 freeze record (accepted 2026-10-21)

P1 behavior is agreed; documentation consistency review is pending. Implement no RTL until the P1 document review is confirmed.

Frozen implementation requirements:
- Use one synthesizable Verilog-2001 controller module, one clock, active-high synchronous reset.
- Suggested states: `IDLE`, `RUNNING`, and `LOCKOUT` with expiry/recheck handled by the lockout counter/state transition. Keep the implementation compact; do not add unnecessary states.
- `dry_run_fault` has priority over demand. `pump_enable` must be low whenever the sampled fault is high and during lockout.
- Start/restart a full `LOCKOUT_CYCLES` interval after detected fault and after every unsuccessful recheck, including demand-low rechecks.
- Clear `fault_status` only on reset or successful recovery/restart; set it on detected fault.
- Reject/document `LOCKOUT_CYCLES < 1`; test `LOCKOUT_CYCLES=1` exactly.
- No generated clocks, delays, analog logic, motor driver, or physical-sensor claims.

After documentation validation, the next authorized step is P1 closeout only. RTL starts only after the user confirms the documents are consistent.
